DATA from Coursera

.the world's most valuable resource 
.collection of facts 
    .numbers/ pictures/ videos/ words/ measurements/ observations etc 
.data analytics
    .the collection, transformation, and organization of data in order to draw conclusions, make predictions, and drive 
    informed decision making 


Data types
.numerical - consists of numbers that can be measured, counted, or used in mathematical calculations 
.text/string data - consists of letters, words, sentences, or a mix od all
    .used as identifiers, not for calculation 
        e.g product name, customer address, notes, ID numbers
.date data - represents specific points in time, such as date or timestamp
    .crucial for tracking trends and events over time 
.categorical data - can be divided into groups or categories 
    .often represents labels, names, or discrete categories 
        e.g product color, rating, customer loyalty status


Steps of DA
.Ask
    .problem statement
    .understand the challenge to be solved 
.Prepare
    .build timeline of course of action 
    .identify the data needed & the sources; verify source accuracy and usefulness in answering questions  
    .develop specific questions
        .establish rules for data access 
            .develop specific info to be gathered 
.Process
    .cleaning & organizing the data 
    .collection, storage, management, and protection of data
        .removing inconsistencies, filling missing values, changing data format 
        .restrict access to the data/ clean it to ensure complete, correct, and relevant/ upload the data to a warehouse to ensure security 
.Analyze
    .gain insights from the data
        .analyze to uncover answers and solutions 
        .examine trends and patterns from the data 
        .document the findings and develop reports  
.Share
    .sharing the report to decision-makers through reporting/ presentation
        .communicate the results with the right context 
.Act 
    .implement changes and take actions based on the findings


